  "english": "17. Monday. Tone 1 [AH] [with abbreviation for Fast? No, \"Բչ. ԱՉԶՉ. Պահք\" - Monday, Tone 1, Fast]. Fast of Advent. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 3 [GY]: \"Blessed art thou\" (Orhneal es).\n\n21. Friday. Tone 2 [GZ]. Fast. Feast of the Presentation of the Holy Mother of God.\n\n23. Sunday. Tone 3 [DZ]. First [Sunday of Advent]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 1 [AY]: \"Blessed art thou, Lord God\" (Orhneal es ter Astuads). Second Canticle [Hambartsi], Tone 3 [GY]: \"Fearful\" (Ahagin), and \"Thou who art above\" (Or i verd es).\n\n24. Monday. Tone 3 [DK]. [Feast of Saints] Juliana and Vasilouhi. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 3 [GY]: \"Who [passed through] the torments\" (Ork ztanjans).\n\n30. Sunday. Tone 3 [GK]. Second [Sunday of Advent]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 1 [AK]: \"Without beginning\" (Anskizbn). Second Canticle [Hambartsi], Tone 3 [GK]: \"Taking\" (Areal). For the others, see in order in the First Volume, keeping the order of this place.\n\nDecember\n\n1. Monday. Tone 4 [DZ]. [Feast of] Bishop Genarios, the soldier Mercurius, and Jacob and Righteous [Iravaparr].\n\n2. Tuesday. Tone 4 [DK]. [Feast of] Cornelius the Centurion, and Shmavon, and the others.\n\n7. Sunday. Tone 3 [GZ]. Third [Sunday of Advent]. Eve of the Fast of Saint James. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 2 [BY]: \"Who art king\" (Or tagavord es). (Second Canticle [Hambartsi], Tone 3 [GY]: \"Glorified is thy\" [Parravoreal e ko]).\n\n9. Tuesday. Tone 4 [DZ]. Fast. Feast of the Conception of the Holy Virgin.\n\n14. Sunday. Tone 2 [BK]. Fourth [Sunday of Advent]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 2 [BK]: \"Who [by the form] of a servant\" (Or ztsarayi). Second Canticle [Hambartsi], Tone 2 [BK]: \"The women forestalled\" (Kankhetsin kanaykn).\n\n21. Sunday. Tone 2 [Bch? / BZ]. Fifth [Sunday of Advent]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 3 [GY]: \"Glorified Son\" (Parravoreal vordi). Second Canticle [Hambartsi], Tone 2 [BY]: \"In the tomb\" (I gerezman), and \"They came to the tomb\" (Ekin i gerezman), and \"That tidings\" (Zayn avetavor), and \"Today they rejoiced\" (Aysor zvartchatsan).\n\n22. Monday. Tone 2 [BK]. [Feast of Saints] Abraham and Khoren, and Cosmas and Damian, and Astuadsatur the Martyr. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 1 [AY]: \"Thee, righteous\" (Zkez ardar).\n\n23. Tuesday. Tone 3 [GD]. [Feast of] David the Prophet and James the Apostle.\n\n24. Wednesday. Tone 3 [GK]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 4 [DK]: \"Blessed be the Lord God, blessed\" (Orhneal ter astuads orhneal).\n\n28. Sunday. Tone 1 [AK]. Sixth [Sunday of Advent]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 3 [GK]: \"From eternity\" (Nakhahavityan). Second Canticle [Hambartsi], Tone 1 [AK]: \"Wondrous Resurrection\" (Hrashali zyaryutyun).\n\n29. Monday. Tone 2 [Bch? / BZ]. [Feast of] the Sons of Thunder [James and John]. Eve of the Fast of the Nativity.\n\n30. Tuesday. Tone 2 [BK]. Fast of the Nativity of Christ. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 4 [DK]: \"Blessed art thou, Lord God of our fathers\" (Orhneal es ter astuads hartsyn). And the rest in order.\n\nJanuary\n\n4. Sunday. Tone 1 [AD]. Seventh [Sunday], Fast. Second Canticle [Hambartsi], Tone 1 [AY]: \"Awesome vision\" (Sokali tesil), to the end.\n\n5. Monday. Tone 1 [AK]. Eve of the Nativity of Christ our God.\n\nThe Roman Cycle of Seven, 2.\n\nJanuary\n\n6. Tuesday [AVURAKE]. Feast of the Nativity and Epiphany of Christ. The period of eating meat [non-fasting days] is fifteen days.\n\n14. Monday. [Feast of] John the Forerunner.\n\n15. Tuesday. [Feast of] Patriarch Peter, Vlas [Blaise], and the others.\n\n17. Thursday. [Feast of] Anton [Anthony] the Anchorite.\n\n19. Saturday. [Feast of] Theodosius the King and the Holy Infants of Ephesus.\n\n20. Sunday. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 4 [DZ]: \"The dawning of the Only-Begotten\" (Tsagumn miadsni). Eve of the Fast of the Catechumens [Arrajavor].\n\n27. Sunday. [Feast of] Saint Sarkis. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 3 [GD]: \"Glorifying\" (Parravorelov). And see the others in the First Volume up to Transfiguration [Vardavar], keeping the order of this place.",
